DXWEB + DXWEB ADMIN - NGINX DEPLOYMENT GUIDE
===========================================

This guide corresponds to DXWeb source v2.8.45 and DXWeb Admin source v0.78.25 and to the supplied
systemd units and Nginx templates. It supersedes the older README-nginx.
No Nginx is needed for the DEFAULT deployment.


DXSPIDER ROOT AND SERVICE TEMPLATES

Set DXSPIDER_ROOT to the actual DXSpider installation directory before
following the commands in this guide. For example:

  export DXSPIDER_ROOT=/home/sysop/spider

On installations using a different root, change this value accordingly.
Do not assume /spider is the active installation.

The supplied systemd templates use /home/sysop/spider as their reference
installation path, with User=sysop and Group=sysop. Before installing a
template, adapt WorkingDirectory and ExecStart to the actual DXSPIDER_ROOT.
For example, generate an adapted unit before installing it:

  sed "s|/home/sysop/spider|$DXSPIDER_ROOT|g" TEMPLATE > /tmp/UNIT

Replace TEMPLATE and UNIT with the corresponding service filenames.
Review the generated unit before installing it. Keep User=sysop and
Group=sysop unless the administrator explicitly chooses another account.
systemd does not expand shell variables in WorkingDirectory.

The DXWeb installer installs application files; it does not install or
configure systemd units or Nginx.

PORTS AND TOPOLOGY (native DXSpider)

Mode                 DXWeb HTTP        Admin HTTP        DXSpider IntMsg
DIRECT (default)     0.0.0.0:7380      0.0.0.0:7381      127.0.0.1:27754
NGINX SAME HOST      127.0.0.1:7480    127.0.0.1:7481    127.0.0.1:27754
Nginx public ports   7380             7381             not proxied

0.0.0.0 is a bind address, not a URL: browse to the server's real IP or DNS name.
The DXSpider technical port 27754 is not the browser port.
Direct Admin on unencrypted HTTP exposes credentials: limit access to a trusted
network, or use a properly configured HTTPS reverse proxy for remote use.

The provided Nginx templates assume Nginx and both web processes share a host.
If Nginx is on ANOTHER server, 127.0.0.1 in proxy_pass points to that other
server, not to DXSpider. These templates are NOT a verified remote-Nginx setup.
Such a deployment requires a separately secured upstream, firewall/TLS design,
and a review of the source-IP and WebSocket Origin trust logic; do not simply
replace 127.0.0.1 with a public address and set MOJO_REVERSE_PROXY=1.

VARIABLES AND TRUST

DXS_HOST (DXWeb only): address of the OUTBOUND DXSpider IntMsg peer; default
127.0.0.1. DXS_PORT: technical port, default 27754. DXWeb Admin's backend
address is fixed to 127.0.0.1 in the reviewed code; DXS_PORT is configurable.

HTTP_HOST / HTTP_PORT (DXWeb): browser listener bind and port.
DXWEB_HOST / DXWEB_PORT (Admin): corresponding Admin listener bind and port.
0.0.0.0 listens on all IPv4 interfaces; 127.0.0.1 is loopback only.

MOJO_REVERSE_PROXY=0 is the default for direct use. With trusted same-host
Nginx set it to 1 in the systemd service environment. It instructs Mojolicious
to interpret reverse-proxy headers; it neither starts Nginx nor changes ports.
The application's WebSocket source-IP/Origin handling also has explicit
loopback-specific checks: do not treat MOJO_REVERSE_PROXY=1 as a generic trust
or security switch. Nginx must overwrite forwarded headers, not pass arbitrary
client-supplied values through. Keep backend ports inaccessible externally.
EXAMPLE FILES (both applications in each file)

  dxweb-http.conf.example   HTTP test/example, NOT suitable for credentials
                             across an untrusted network.
  dxweb-https.conf.example  HTTPS/WSS; requires real TLS cert/key files.
  dxweb-subdir-https.conf.example  HTTPS/WSS mounted at /dxweb/ and
                             /dxweb-admin/ on a shared HTTPS listener 443.

Use exactly ONE layout for a given public listener; don't enable conflicting
server blocks. The templates assume both applications and Nginx share a host.
For production, prefer HTTPS; restrict Admin access to authorized networks.

STEP 1 - SERVICES

Back up the current service units. Install both *.service.nginx.example units
as dxweb.service and dxweb-admin.service under /etc/systemd/system. They bind
127.0.0.1:7480 and :7481 with MOJO_REVERSE_PROXY=1. Reload systemd and
restart only dxweb and dxweb-admin. Do not restart DXSpider.

  cd "$DXSPIDER_ROOT"
  cp -p /etc/systemd/system/dxweb.service /root/dxweb.service.before-nginx
  cp -p /etc/systemd/system/dxweb-admin.service /root/dxweb-admin.service.before-nginx
  sed "s|/home/sysop/spider|$DXSPIDER_ROOT|g" dxweb.service.nginx.example > /tmp/dxweb.service
  systemd-analyze verify /tmp/dxweb.service
  install -m 0644 /tmp/dxweb.service /etc/systemd/system/dxweb.service
  sed "s|/home/sysop/spider|$DXSPIDER_ROOT|g" dxweb-admin.service.nginx.example > /tmp/dxweb-admin.service
  systemd-analyze verify /tmp/dxweb-admin.service
  install -m 0644 /tmp/dxweb-admin.service /etc/systemd/system/dxweb-admin.service
  systemctl daemon-reload
  systemctl restart dxweb.service dxweb-admin.service
  curl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:7480/healthz
  curl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:7481/healthz

STEP 2 - NGINX

Edit the FQDN placeholder (and real certificate paths in HTTPS examples).
Install ONE example, for example:
  install -m 0644 $DXSPIDER_ROOT/dxweb/docs/dxweb-https.conf.example /etc/nginx/sites-available/dxweb.conf
  ln -sfn /etc/nginx/sites-available/dxweb.conf /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/dxweb.conf
  nginx -t
  systemctl reload nginx

If a site already exists, back it up before overwriting. Check for conflicts
with default sites and other server blocks. The HTTP example is intended for
restricted testing only, not Internet-facing authenticated use.

ROOT MODE

  https://YOUR_FQDN:7380/  -> Nginx -> 127.0.0.1:7480 (DXWeb)
  https://YOUR_FQDN:7381/  -> Nginx -> 127.0.0.1:7481 (Admin)

SUBDIRECTORY MODE (optional, separate template)

  https://YOUR_FQDN/dxweb/       -> 127.0.0.1:7480/
  https://YOUR_FQDN/dxweb-admin/ -> 127.0.0.1:7481/

Use trailing slashes on the public base paths. In Nginx, proxy_pass with a
trailing slash removes the external prefix before forwarding to Mojolicious.
The DXWeb and DXWeb Admin HTML and JS use relative URLs for static assets and WebSockets.
This layout still REQUIRES live browser validation (login, assets, websocket,
console, filters) and has not been certified in this environment.

SECURITY / FORWARDED HEADERS

The proxy overwrites Host, X-Real-IP, X-Forwarded-For and X-Forwarded-Proto.
Do not trust forwarded headers from arbitrary clients. MOJO_REVERSE_PROXY=1
is ONLY for trusted proxy mode. Nginx must handle Upgrade/Connection for
WebSockets; the backend must not be directly reachable by untrusted users.
Browser Origin validation compares scheme, host and port. When testing,
use the actual public hostname, port and scheme, not an unrelated Origin.

STEP 3 - CHECK

  nginx -t
  ss -ltnp | grep -E ':(7380|7381|7480|7481|443) '
  curl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:7480/healthz
  curl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:7481/healthz

For HTTPS verify with a valid certificate and DNS, then test actual browser
WebSocket, authentication and client IP. Never treat curl success as a full
end-to-end test. For rollback restore the backed-up systemd units, run
systemctl daemon-reload and restart both web services, then disable the
Nginx site if it conflicts with the restored direct listeners.

